# Binary Block — core separation (Phase 1.1)

## Layout

- `core/` — UI-free: `block` · `levelData` · `board` · `rules` · `pieces` · `level` · `session`
- `ui/` — React only (input → core → render)
- `puzzle/` — thin adapters (binary text, scoring, legacy re-exports)
- Level JSON lives in `levels/levels.json`; access via `core/levelData` (no per-level `if`)

## Dependency direction (never reverse)

```
block / levelData / board → rules → level/session → (future) solver → analyzer → generator
```

Do **not** create empty `solver.ts` / `generator.ts` / `analyzer.ts` until that phase.

## Rules

- No React / DOM / Audio / localStorage / network inside `core/`
- Place / rotate / board bootstrap go through `core/session` (`tryPlacePiece`, `tryRotatePiece`, `createSessionBoard`)
- Do not delete or rewrite AudioManager work
- Prefer minimal adapters over copying logic back into UI
- Capacity first — no new npm deps, no unused stubs
